(8,23,18,'Fomite','An object or surface, like a doorknob or phone, that can carry pathogens.',false,true),
(8,23,19,'Antibiotic','A medicine that kills or stops bacteria; it does not work on viruses.',false,true),
(8,23,20,'Memory cells','Immune cells that remember a pathogen so the body responds faster if it returns.',false,true),
(8,24,21,'Sexually transmitted infection','An infection passed from person to person through sexual contact; also called STD.',false,false),
(8,24,22,'Asymptomatic','Showing no symptoms despite being infected — makes STIs especially dangerous.',false,false),
(8,24,23,'HPV','Human Papillomavirus — the most common STI; high-risk strains cause cancer. Prevented by Gardasil 9.',false,false),
(8,24,24,'Chlamydia','The most reported bacterial STI; mostly asymptomatic; curable with antibiotics; untreated causes infertility.',false,false),
(8,24,25,'Gonorrhea','The second most common bacterial STI; drug resistance is a growing crisis.',false,false),
(8,24,26,'Syphilis','Progresses through stages; congenital syphilis up 700% over the past decade; curable with penicillin.',false,false),
(8,24,27,'HIV','Human Immunodeficiency Virus — attacks CD4+ T cells, progressively destroying the immune system.',false,false),
(8,24,28,'AIDS','Acquired Immunodeficiency Syndrome — the final stage of HIV infection.',false,false),
(8,24,29,'Antiretroviral therapy','The combination of medications that suppress HIV replication — allows near-normal lifespan.',false,false),
(8,24,30,'U=U','Undetectable equals Untransmittable — people with HIV on effective ART cannot sexually transmit the virus.',false,false),
(8,24,31,'PrEP','Pre-Exposure Prophylaxis — reduces HIV transmission risk from sex by ~99% when taken as prescribed.',false,false),
(8,24,32,'Gardasil 9','The current HPV vaccine covering 9 strains — recommended for all people ages 9–26.',false,false),
(8,24,33,'Abstinence','Refraining from sexual activity; the only 100% effective method to prevent STIs and pregnancy.',false,true),
(8,24,34,'Herpes','A viral STI with no cure that can be managed with medicine.',false,false),
(8,24,35,'Hepatitis B','A viral infection of the liver that can spread sexually; a vaccine prevents it.',false,false),
(8,24,36,'Trichomoniasis','A common parasitic STI that is treatable with medicine.',false,false),
(8,24,37,'CD4 T-cells','Immune system "commander" cells that HIV attacks.',false,false),
(8,24,38,'Partner notification','Letting partners know about a possible STI exposure so they can get tested; health departments can do it anonymously.',false,false),
(8,24,39,'Stigma','Negative attitudes that keep people from getting tested, treated or telling partners.',false,true),
(8,24,40,'STI testing','Medical tests that show whether a person has an STI; the only way to know your status.',false,false),
(8,25,41,'Noncommunicable disease','A disease that cannot be spread from person to person.',false,true),
(8,25,42,'Cardiovascular disease','Any disease affecting the heart or blood vessels; the leading cause of death in the U.S.',false,true),
(8,25,43,'Hypertension','Chronically elevated blood pressure (130/80 or above per 2017 AHA guidelines); the ''silent killer''.',false,true),
(8,25,44,'Atherosclerosis','A disease in which fatty plaques accumulate on artery walls, narrowing and hardening them.',false,true),
(8,25,45,'Stroke','An acute injury in which blood flow to part of the brain is interrupted — requires immediate 911 response.',false,true),
(8,25,46,'Cancer','A disease characterized by the uncontrolled growth and spread of abnormal cells.',false,true),
(8,25,47,'Tumor','An abnormal mass of tissue; may be benign (non-cancerous) or malignant (cancerous).',false,true),
(8,25,48,'Metastasis','The spread of cancer from its original location to other parts of the body.',false,true),
(8,25,49,'Remission','A period when cancer is undetectable or under control.',false,true),
(8,25,50,'Diabetes','A chronic disease in which the body cannot properly regulate blood glucose.',false,true),
(8,25,51,'Allergy','An immune system overreaction to a normally harmless substance (allergen).',false,true),
(8,25,52,'Americans with Disabilities Act','The 1990 federal law prohibiting discrimination against people with disabilities.',false,true),
(8,25,53,'Malignant','Describes a tumor that is cancerous and has the potential to invade other tissues.',false,true),
(8,25,54,'Insulin','The hormone that allows cells to absorb glucose from the bloodstream for energy.',false,true),
(8,25,55,'Disability','A physical, mental, or developmental condition that limits one or more major life activities.',false,true),
(8,25,56,'Benign','A tumor that is not cancerous and does not invade other tissues.',false,true),
(8,25,57,'Type 1 diabetes','An autoimmune disease in which the immune system destroys insulin-producing cells; it requires insulin.',false,true),
(8,25,58,'Type 2 diabetes','A disease in which cells resist insulin; it is often linked to inactivity and excess weight and is largely preventable.',false,true),
(8,25,59,'Prediabetes','Blood sugar higher than normal but below the diabetic level; a signal to change habits.',false,true),
(8,25,60,'People-first language','Speaking about the person before the condition, such as "person with a disability.".',false,true),
(8,25,61,'Assistive technology','Tools such as wheelchairs, hearing aids and screen readers that increase independence.',false,true),
(9,26,1,'Personal safety','The steps you take to reduce your risk of becoming a victim of crime.',false,true),
(9,26,2,'Cyberbullying','The use of digital technology to harass, humiliate, or threaten — affects ~46% of teens.',false,true),
(9,26,3,'Accident chain','The predictable sequence: unsafe situation → unsafe habit → unsafe action = accident.',false,true),
(9,26,4,'Defensive driving','Driving with awareness of potential hazards and taking proactive action to avoid them.',false,true),
(9,26,5,'Road rage','Responding to driving incidents with aggression or violence.',false,true),
(9,26,6,'Graduated licensing','A staged system that increases driving privileges as new drivers build experience.',false,true),
(9,26,7,'Personal flotation device','A life jacket or other approved device that keeps a person afloat — required for boating.',false,true),
(9,26,8,'OSHA','The Occupational Safety and Health Administration — the federal agency responsible for workplace safety.',false,true),
(9,26,9,'Fire safety','Practices to prevent and respond to fires — smoke alarms, extinguishers, and escape plans.',false,true),
(9,26,10,'Distracted driving','Operating a vehicle while attention is diverted — texting is the most dangerous form.',false,true),
(9,26,11,'Accident','An unintended event that results in injury, damage, or harm.',false,true),
(9,26,12,'Concussion','A mild traumatic brain injury caused by a blow or jolt to the head that temporarily disrupts brain function.',false,true),
(9,26,13,'Second impact syndrome','A rare but often fatal condition where a second concussion occurs before the first has healed.',false,true),
(9,26,14,'Heat exhaustion','A heat-related illness caused by overheating, involving heavy sweating, weakness, and dizziness.',false,true),
(9,26,15,'Heat stroke','A life-threatening condition where body temperature exceeds 104°F; requires immediate emergency care.',false,true),
(9,26,16,'Fire escape plan','A prepared strategy for evacuating a building safely during a fire, practiced regularly by household members.',false,true),
(9,26,17,'Passive safety','Safety measures that protect automatically without requiring action (e.g., airbags, smoke alarms).',false,true),
(9,26,18,'Active safety','Safety measures that require deliberate human action (e.g., wearing a seat belt, using a helmet).',false,true),
(9,26,19,'Seat belt','A safety restraint that cuts crash death risk by about 45% in the front seat and 60% in the back.',false,true),
(9,26,20,'Emergency kit','A 72-hour supply of water, food, medicine, a flashlight and first aid for disasters.',false,true),
